<article>
  <p>If you like metaphors and network gadgets that act like sneaky middle managers then this is for you. Forward proxies are the user cloak that hides who is knocking on the web s door. Reverse proxies are the server bouncer that decides which backend gets in and which one waits outside in the rain. Both meddle with traffic and both keep logs that tell different stories.</p>

</article>

